\name{cellucid_analysis_view_set}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_view_set}
\title{Change how an analysis is shown}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_view_set(viewer, analysis, view, in_ = "panel")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{analysis}{An analysis with an options form. One of \code{"markers"}, \code{"differential"}, \code{"dotplot"}, \code{"signature"}, \code{"composition"}, \code{"correlation"}. Required.}
\item{view}{What to change of how the analysis is shown (only the keys given). A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{group}}{Marker genes: the group its expanded table lists, by name (null: the first tested group). Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Optional.}\item{\code{groups}}{The option groups open inside "More options", by id (every other is closed). A vector or list of one of \code{"groups"}, \code{"test"}, \code{"filters"}, \code{"ranking"}, \code{"cells"}, \code{"labels"}, \code{"values"}, \code{"layout"}, \code{"scoring"}, \code{"display"} (each once). Optional.}\item{\code{heatmap}}{Marker genes: the heatmap's look and clustering (only the keys given). A named list. Optional. \describe{\item{\code{clusterCols}}{\code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Optional.}\item{\code{clusterRows}}{\code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Optional.}\item{\code{colorscale}}{One of \code{"RdBu"}, \code{"Viridis"}, \code{"Blues"}, \code{"YlOrRd"}, \code{"Greens"}. Optional.}\item{\code{distance}}{One of \code{"correlation"}, \code{"euclidean"}, \code{"cosine"}. Optional.}\item{\code{linkage}}{One of \code{"average"}, \code{"complete"}, \code{"single"}. Optional.}\item{\code{transform}}{One of \code{"zscore"}, \code{"log1p"}, \code{"none"}. Optional.}}}\item{\code{more}}{Whether its "More options" are open. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Optional.}\item{\code{plot}}{Options of the plot its expanded view draws, each by its name and value as the expanded view offers it. A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Optional.}\item{\code{set}}{Gene signature: the gene set a result of one score per set shows, by name. Text (at least 1 character). Optional.}\item{\code{show}}{Marker genes: what the result shows. One of \code{"list"}, \code{"heatmap"}, \code{"clustered"}. Optional.}}}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Open or close its option groups, and choose what its result shows (marker genes: list or heatmap, the group listed, the heatmap's look; gene signature: the set shown; the options of the plot its expanded view draws); nothing runs.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.view.set} (Analysis). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{analysis}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_view_set(viewer, analysis = "markers",
      view = list(show = "list"))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
